# Earshot

Earshot captures voice-first user feedback from this app. Each report bundles a transcript, screenshot, DOM/console/network context, captured user identity, and a clarifying-agent dialog. The Earshot MCP server at `https://mcp.earshotbot.com/mcp` exposes the same surface the dashboard uses, scoped to this project by the `pk_*` Bearer token in `.cursor/mcp.json`.

## When to call these tools

Use the `earshot` MCP server when the user mentions:

- "the inbox" / "feedback" / "bug reports" / "user reports"
- A specific feedback id (`fb_*`)
- "clarify" / "follow up with the user" / "ask them more"
- "push the project context" / "update Earshot's brief" / "tell Earshot about ..."
- Triage, resolution, comments, labels, status changes on feedback

If the user describes a bug they just fixed and there's an open feedback item that matches, call `resolve_feedback` with a note. If the user asks "what's in the inbox?", call `list_feedback`.

## Tool reference

All tools listed below are project-scoped via the `pk_*` key in `.cursor/mcp.json`. Tool names match `apps/mcp/src/mcp/tools.ts` verbatim.

### Triage

- **`list_feedback`** — newest-first list. Filter by `status` (one or many of `triage` / `backlog` / `in_progress` / `done` / `canceled`). Returns id, title, summary, status, priority, labels, identity, created_at, plus `next_cursor` for pagination. Default to `status: ['triage']` when the user says "the inbox".
- **`get_feedback`** — full record by `fb_*` id. Includes voice transcript, clarify dialog, captured page/device/console/network, identity, federation, external tracker link.
- **`list_comments`** — comment thread on a feedback item, oldest first.

### Action

- **`resolve_feedback`** — mark resolved with a note. Stamps `resolved_at`, adds an audit comment authored by the agent, mirrors to the linked tracker, emails the submitter if identity captured + Resend configured. Call this when the user says "I fixed it" or "this is done."
- **`clarify_feedback`** — run Earshot's hosted clarifying agent on demand. Pass a `feedback_id`. Optionally pass `user_answer` to add a new user turn, or `agent_question` to force a specific follow-up. Returns either `{action:'ask', question}` (bounce to user) or `{action:'finalize', record}`. Use this instead of burning the agent's context window asking follow-ups directly.

### Project context

Push the host app's stack, routes, glossary, personas, known issues, and recent changes so Earshot's clarifying agent can ground its follow-ups in this product, not just the DOM.

- **`get_project_context`** — read current context before deciding to update or supplement.
- **`set_project_context`** — push/replace/deep-merge the brief. Argument `replace: false` deep-merges by section; `replace: true` (default) replaces the whole brief.
- **`validate_project_context`** — dry-run a context payload (checks token budget) before pushing.
- **`list_project_context_revisions`** — audit log.

### Integrations

- **`suggest_integrations`** — advisor-only. Pass detected services from the host repo; returns a ranked plan.
- **`connect_integration`** — commit one integration (Linear, Jira, PostHog, Sentry, LogRocket, Datadog). Credentials encrypted at rest with AES-256-GCM. Returns id + `credential_summary` with last-4 chars of sensitive fields only.
- **`test_integration`** — smoke-test the credentials against the provider's API.
- **`list_integrations`** — list integrations on this project. Never includes credentials.

## Default workflows

### "Triage the inbox"

1. `list_feedback({ status: ['triage'], limit: 20 })`
2. For each item the user wants to act on: `get_feedback({ id })`
3. If the agent needs more info from the submitter: `clarify_feedback({ feedback_id: id, agent_question: '...' })` — Earshot handles the follow-up loop.
4. When fix is shipped: `resolve_feedback({ id, resolution_note: 'Fixed in PR #...' })`

### "Tell Earshot about my app"

1. `get_project_context()` — see what's there.
2. Compile updated brief from this repo (`package.json`, `README.md`, routes, schema, common error patterns).
3. `validate_project_context({ sections, body })` — confirm token budget.
4. `set_project_context({ sections, body, replace: false })` — deep-merge.

## Limits

- `pk_*` is project-scoped: tools that create teams/projects (`create_team`, `create_project`, `rotate_api_key`, `list_projects`) require user-scoped OAuth and are NOT available with this key. Use the dashboard at `https://app.earshotbot.com` for those operations.
- All MCP tool errors include a structured `error` field. Surface the message to the user verbatim — do not retry blindly on 401/403.